silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_01_patch_cover_cocone_sections_04_mittens_patch_anchor_yoneda_hom_leg a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "04MittensPatchAnchorYonedaHomLegExample" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_01_patch_cover_cocone_sections_04_mittens_patch_anchor_yoneda_hom_leg silm:hasExample "In '04MittensPatchAnchorYonedaHomLeg', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, In 'The Mittens Patch Anchor' the typed_patch_inclusion arrow witnesses the head patch U_head is included into the Mittens diagram image I_Mittens as a typed sub-region preserving the cat-classification node; this typed leg is load-bearing for the mittens patch anchor step of the topology-JEPA pipeline.; also, In 'The Mittens Patch Anchor' the overlap_restriction_head arrow witnesses the overlap zone restricts the head patch hypothesis to the shared neck-joint region, the sheaf-restriction arrow forced by patch overlap; this typed leg is load-bearing for the mittens patch anchor step of the topology-JEPA pipeline." .
